raudio: loop points for a looping Music, stopping a paused stream, pausing the device,
unloading a FLAC music, a null device without audio hardware

Music gets a loop region, loopStart and loopEnd (frames, end excluded; 0, the
default: the whole music loops). A looping music decodes up to loopEnd, then
goes on from loopStart, sample-exactly: UpdateMusicStream() reads the decoded
formats (WAV, OGG, MP3, QOA, FLAC) through one loop, ReadMusicFrames() and
SeekMusicDecoder(). GetMusicTimePlayed() and SeekMusicStream() wrap into the
loop region the same way.

SeekMusicStream() seeks OGG sample-exactly (stb_vorbis_seek(), not
stb_vorbis_seek_frame()), and seeks the decoder under the audio lock, which
UpdateMusicStream() decodes under.

StopAudioBufferInLockedState() also stops a paused buffer: it stayed paused,
and resumed where it was, StopMusicStream() having rewound its decoder.

PauseAudioDevice() / ResumeAudioDevice() stop and start the miniaudio device:
nothing plays meanwhile, and every sound and music goes on where it was (an
Android application in the background).

UnloadMusicStream() of a FLAC music freed its decoder twice: drflac_close()
frees it already (SUPPORT_FILEFORMAT_FLAC is off by default upstream).

InitAudioDevice() falls back to miniaudio's null backend when the default
playback device cannot be opened (no sound card: a server, a CI runner):
the audio API stays usable, sounds and musics played into nothing at their
own pace, as OpenAL Soft's null output. raylib gave up, IsAudioDeviceReady()
false, and nothing could be loaded.

